### ML Model Stack

```
Input Text
    ↓
Tokenizer → Token Sequence
    ↓
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Classical ML (TF-IDF)            │
│ • IntentClassifierSimple         │
│ • EntityExtractor (BIO tagging)  │
│ • POSTagger (HMM-based)          │
│ • Gazetteer (ETS lookup)         │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
    ↓
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ LSTM Models (Axon/Nx/EXLA)       │
│ Shared BiLSTM Encoder            │
│ ├── Intent Head (UnifiedModel)   │
│ ├── NER Head (UnifiedModel)      │
│ ├── Sentiment Head (UnifiedModel)│
│ ├── Speech Act Head (Unified)    │
│ └── POS Head (MultiTaskModel)    │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
    ↓
LSTMIntegration (Ensemble: TF-IDF + LSTM when confidence < 0.6)
    ↓
Response Generation → LSTMResponse (response scoring)
    ↓
Best Response Selected
```

## Common Patterns

### GenServer Ready Check Pattern

```elixir
def ready?(name \\ __MODULE__) do
  try do
    GenServer.call(name, :ready?, 100)
  catch
    :exit, _ -> false
  end
end

# Before using the GenServer
if UnifiedModel.ready?() do
  UnifiedModel.classify_sentiment(text)
else
  %{label: :neutral, confidence: 0.5}
end
```

### Model Reload Pattern

LSTM GenServers support hot-reloading after retraining:

```elixir
Brain.ML.LSTM.UnifiedModel.reload()
Brain.ML.LSTM.MultiTaskModel.reload()
Brain.Response.LSTMResponse.reload()
```

### Slot Detection for Missing Context

```elixir
# In slot_schemas.json
"weather.query": {
  "required": ["location"],
  "clarification_templates": {
    "location": "What location would you like the weather for?"
  }
}
```

### Multi-Sentence Response Combination

```elixir
# 1. Semantic chunker splits into sentences
# 2. Each chunk analyzed in parallel (discourse + speech act + sentiment)
# 3. Response strategies combined:
#    - :can_respond + :needs_clarification = :partial_response_with_clarification
# 4. Brain combines greeting response + substantive response
```

## Important Files

### Configuration

- `priv/analysis/slot_schemas.json` - Required/optional slots per intent
- `data/intents/*.json` - Training data for intent classification
- `data/entities/*.json` - Entity definitions for gazetteer
- `priv/ml_models/` - Trained classical model files (`.term`)
- `priv/ml_models/lstm/` - LSTM model files + `experiments.json`
- `priv/evaluation/` - Gold standard data + evaluation results

### Training

```bash
mix train                          # Master pipeline (all models)
mix train --quick                  # Skip slow models
mix train --name "experiment_v1"   # Track experiment
mix train --compare                # Show experiment comparison

mix train_unified                  # Unified LSTM (intent + NER + sentiment + speech act)
mix train_response                 # Response scorer LSTM
mix train_lstm                     # Standalone LSTM intent classifier
mix train_models                   # TF-IDF + optional LSTM
```

### Evaluation

```bash
mix evaluate                       # Evaluate all tasks
mix evaluate.intent --save         # Intent classification with save
mix evaluate.sentiment --verbose   # Sentiment with per-class details
mix evaluate.speech_act            # Speech act classification
mix evaluate.ner                   # Named entity recognition

mix test --only benchmark          # Run accuracy threshold tests
```

### Model Regeneration

```bash
mix regenerate_test_models --check    # Check Nx/Axon compatibility
mix regenerate_test_models --all      # Regenerate all test models
```

## Routes

| Route | LiveView | Purpose |
|-------|----------|---------|
| `/chat` | ChatLive | Main chat + processing inspector |
| `/dashboard` | DashboardLive | System monitoring, GenServers, metrics |
| `/accuracy` | AccuracyLive | Model accuracy, confusion matrices, trends |
| `/explorer` | ExplorerLive | Training world data (entities, episodes, knowledge) |
| `/settings` | SettingsLive | World/entity management, ML training controls |
| `/code` | CodeAnalysisLive | Code symbol browser |
| `/intent-review` | IntentReviewLive | Novel intent candidate review |
| `/knowledge-review` | KnowledgeReviewLive | Knowledge expansion review |

## Testing

### Running Tests

```bash
mix test                           # All tests (excludes slow, benchmark, gpu)
mix test --only benchmark          # Accuracy threshold tests
mix test --only integration        # Integration tests
mix test --exclude requires_lstm   # Skip LSTM-dependent tests
```

### Test Helpers

- `test/support/lstm_test_helpers.ex` - Model compatibility checking, test model generation
- Tests use real models with graceful degradation when models are incompatible
- `@moduletag :benchmark` for accuracy threshold tests (excluded by default)

## Code Style

### Elixir Conventions

- **No regex for text processing** - use `Tokenizer` functions
- **No `String.contains?` for NLP** - use trained classifiers
- GenServers for stateful processes
- ETS for fast concurrent lookups (Gazetteer, world context cache)
- Pattern matching over conditionals when possible
- `Task.async` for parallel work in the pipeline

### Phoenix/LiveView

- Use `<Layouts.app>` wrapper in templates
- Use `<.input>` and `<.form>` components
- WorldContext on_mount hook for persistent world selection
- PubSub topics: `brain:status`, `brain:learning`, `brain:conversations`, `training:progress`
- No inline `<script>` tags - use app.js hooks
- Tailwind CSS + daisyUI for styling

### ML Framework Stack

- `Nx` ~0.7 - Numerical computing
- `Axon` ~0.6 - Neural network framework
- `EXLA` ~0.7 - XLA compiler backend (GPU acceleration)
- `Scholar` ~0.3 - Statistical/ML functions
- Erlang `:erlang.binary_to_term` / `term_to_binary` for model serialization

## Quick Reference

```bash
mix phx.server                     # Start dev server
iex -S mix phx.server              # Start with IEx

mix train --name "v1" --compare    # Train + track experiment
mix evaluate --save --compare      # Evaluate + save + compare

Brain.SystemStatus.get_all()       # Check all statuses
Brain.ML.LSTM.UnifiedModel.ready?()
Brain.ML.CorpusManager.corpus_size()
```

```elixir
# Test analysis pipeline
Brain.Analysis.Pipeline.process("Hello! What's the weather in NYC?")

# Test intent classification
Brain.ML.IntentClassifierSimple.classify("What's the weather?")

# Test LSTM sentiment
Brain.ML.LSTM.UnifiedModel.classify_sentiment("I love this!")

# Test slot detection
Brain.Analysis.SlotDetector.detect("weather.query", [])

# Test evaluation
Brain.ML.Evaluation.accuracy(predictions, actuals)
```
